menu "Ye display"
config YE_LCD_SPI_MHZ
    int "ST7735 SPI clock (MHz)"
    range 1 80
    default 27
    help
        Requested SPI clock. Hardware may round to a supported divider.
        ESP32 supports up to 80 MHz; the attached panel and wiring may not.
        If pixels corrupt on long wires, try 20 or 10 MHz.
config YE_LCD_TARGET_FPS
    int "Animation target FPS"
    range 10 100
    default 60
    help
        Animation scheduling target, not a measured panel refresh rate.
endmenu

menu "Ye Wi-Fi sharing"
config YE_ROUTER_TCP_MSS
    int "Maximum forwarded TCP MSS"
    range 536 1460
    default 1360
    help
        Clamp existing MSS options in IPv4 SYN/SYN-ACK to reduce path-MTU stalls.
        This does not change the MTU or datagram size of a UDP VPN transport.
config YE_NAPT_UDP_TIMEOUT_SECONDS
    int "UDP NAT idle timeout (seconds)"
    range 10 600
    default 120
    help
        Keep idle UDP mappings for proxy/VPN transports. The SDK default is 2s.
        Longer timeouts retain more mappings; check the NAPT capacity counters.
config YE_NAPT_CAPACITY
    int "Maximum shared IPv4 connections"
    range 128 1024
    default 512
    help
        NAPT shares TCP/UDP/ICMP mappings between all hotspot clients.
        A full table can evict an established TCP connection and send RST.
        512 entries use about 8 KiB more RAM than the earlier 256-entry limit.
config YE_NAPT_TCP_TRANSIENT_SECONDS
    int "TCP unfinished/closed NAT idle timeout (seconds)"
    range 5 120
    default 15
    help
        Reclaim idle handshakes, reset connections and fully acknowledged FIN
        connections sooner than the SDK default TCP_MSL (60s).
        Established active TCP connections keep the original 30-minute idle timeout.
config YE_WIFI_HT40
    bool "Allow 40 MHz Wi-Fi bandwidth"
    default y
    help
        Allow HT40 on station and SoftAP, retaining 802.11b/g/n compatibility.
        Actual bandwidth depends on peer negotiation and the upstream channel.
        Disable this option to use HT20 in crowded 2.4 GHz environments.
endmenu
